From fa3edb8c886922aba1e6d2fefdf323b9847c2048 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rawdanger-recomp <rawdanger-recomp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:46:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rawdanger-recomp: v0.8.1 filter replay, texture switch at
 area load, arrows, icons, lens rain

- Colour filter: the first page is drawn the game's way while its steps are written down, then replayed in one pass (CPU or
  GPU) for the rest: two or three depth palettes, writes from palettes or a flat colour (AREA 01's variant was drawn wrong);
  unknown steps fall back to the game's own draws. Byte-identical frames in both variants tested.
- ps2::set_game_filter_pass: one GPU pass or the game's own draws (F1 > Picture, keys.ini post_processing) to compare
- Texture options switched in an area wait for the next area load (PS2_AREA_LOAD), so the characters do not garble
- Built-in fixes are no longer listed; the game's options change with left / right; clicks on a line's < > step it
- Window icon (PS2_WINDOW_ICON, else resource 1) and PS2_EXE_ICON built into ps2run.exe
- Lens rain: drops follow the player's movement (PS2_LENS_MOTION) and look like water (no dark ring, mild lens)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QNLFPekqhcU2dj7B3Utmea
